# WHAT IS COMMITTED HERE, AND WHY IT IS NOT EVERYTHING (playhead-vk68m R4).
#
# Full-plan logs are 13-17 MB each and the per-sample descriptor dumps ran to
# 345 files / 7 MiB, of which exactly ONE was ever cited. Committing them
# established a second in-tree artifact convention competing with
# ~/playhead-gate-artifacts/, which this repo already uses — so the bulk lives
# there (`vk68m-run{1,2,3}-fd-samples.tar.gz`, and the three preserved gate
# logs), and what is committed here is what the write-up actually reads:
#
#   * MEASUREMENTS.md            — the write-up itself
#   * run*/summary.jsonl         — the per-sample time series every number
#                                  in M1a/M4/M9 is derived from (small)
#   * run*/last.json, peak.json  — the tail and peak snapshots
#   * run1/TAIL-453.json         — the dump M1b's table decomposes, in full
#   * run1/cited/               — the three individual samples cited BY NAME
#                                  in source or prose (0001 and 0062 bound the
#                                  leftover-app span in pin_decision's
#                                  docstring; 0094 is the tail)
#   * fd-ceiling-sweep.csv       — M2's table, regenerable by the sweep
#
# The rest is reproducible from the archives, and `git worktree remove` is why
# they live outside the worktree at all: the canonical bead-close sequence
# deletes this directory.
*.log
wait*.txt
run*/full/
